text:
{
"opening": "This release refines the parsing engine to better align with standard format syntax expectations and expands datetime handling capabilities. It addresses several regressions in alignment and digit field numbering while introducing new features for datetime formatting and flexible field naming.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m01",
"text": "The Parser must correctly match input strings that end with a trailing newline character without failing or misinterpreting the final field."
},
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The Parser must correctly handle fields using numeric indices for argument unpacking and support type specifiers within those numbered fields."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The extract_format function must recognize and process sign specifiers (such as '+' or '-') within number format specifications."
},
{
"id": "m05",
"text": "The Parser must revert previous changes to unused alignment handling, restoring behavior that supports verbose use cases where format reversibility is not guaranteed."
},
{
"id": "m18",
"text": "The module must expose dt_format_to_regex, get_regex_for_datetime_format, date_convert, strf_date_convert, and update Parser, TooManyFields, and extract_format to support C standard datetime format codes, including flexible handling of single-digit days/months, colons in time formats, and variable-length %z timezone offsets."
},
{
"id": "m22",
"text": "The Parser class must expose a 'format' property that returns the original format string used to create the parser instance."
},
{
"id": "m24",
"text": "Datetime parsing for the %f directive must support timestamps with varying numbers of digits after the decimal point, such as milliseconds or microseconds."
},
{
"id": "m26",
"text": "The Parser and extract_format must allow hyphen-minus characters (-) within field names during parsing."
},
{
"id": "m33",
"text": "The Parser and extract_format must support grouping characters (commas and underscores) within decimal format strings for improved readability."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all public APIs mentioned above are stable and documented according to these behavioral requirements before tagging the release."
}
